# An atom in the data part of a callable refers to the record its word names, without expansion (plan M11 5a and 5b):
# the Alias of f's data holds the atom code, the part code of f -- `length(f\data\Alias\code)` equals `length(f\code)`,
# 3 -- and the dump keeps `Alias: code` as written.
fn: f () int (Alias: code)
    int: a 1
    int: b 2
    return: 1
int: n length(f\code)
int: m length(f\data\Alias\code)
